  "content": {
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "order": 1,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s1",
            "text": "Sea monsters are not just imaginary."
          },
          {
            "id": "s2",
            "text": "Millions of years ago, real monsters actually lived on Earth."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "order": 2,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s3",
            "text": "Temnodontosaurus was definitely an unusual animal."
          },
          {
            "id": "s4",
            "text": "Its name means “cutting tooth lizard,” and with good reason—it had very big teeth."
          },
          {
            "id": "s5",
            "text": "It also had some of the largest eyes in nature."
          },
          {
            "id": "s6",
            "text": "They were over 25 centimeters across!"
          },
          {
            "id": "s7",
            "text": "With such big eyes, Temnodontosaurus could easily find its food in the dark water."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "order": 3,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s8",
            "text": "Kronosaurus—the “Kronos lizard”—lived in the seas that once covered Australia."
          },
          {
            "id": "s9",
            "text": "But it probably used its fins to climb out of the water and lay its eggs on land."
          },
          {
            "id": "s10",
            "text": "Its head was two meters long, and its teeth were as big as bananas!"
          },
          {
            "id": "s11",
            "text": "The main purpose of strong jaws and teeth like these was to catch smaller animals."
          },
          {
            "id": "s12",
            "text": "In fact, Kronosaurus was one of the most dangerous predators of all time."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "order": 4,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s13",
            "text": "Known as the “lord of the seas,” Thalassomedon was a large sea monster with a very long neck."
          },
          {
            "id": "s14",
            "text": "It also had a special way of hunting fish: It carried stones in its stomach!"
          },
          {
            "id": "s15",
            "text": "These helped keep the largest part of its body and tail down in the dark water."
          },
          {
            "id": "s16",
            "text": "Meanwhile, its long neck slowly rose up toward the fish."
          },
          {
            "id": "s17",
            "text": "The fish didn’t have a chance to get away from Thalassomedon."
          },
          {
            "id": "s18",
            "text": "They couldn’t see the sea monster until it was too late!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "order": 5,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s20",
            "text": "2 To stalk someone or something is to follow slowly and quietly."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
